1
00:00:01,167 --> 00:00:02,967
<i>I reminded Parak of your order
to kill Delgado.</i>

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:03,967
<i>It seems he doesn't want
to do it.</i>

3
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:04,833
<i> I know he will.</i>

4
00:00:04,967 --> 00:00:06,000
<i> He's never let us down.</i>

5
00:00:06,133 --> 00:00:07,233
<i> Your protection here.</i>

6
00:00:07,367 --> 00:00:08,833
<i> Who's going to kill me?</i>

7
00:00:08,967 --> 00:00:10,100
<i> I am thinking, Diego,</i>

8
00:00:10,233 --> 00:00:10,900
<i>you're the one
who's going to do it.</i>

9
00:00:11,033 --> 00:00:12,267
<i>I might get in danger with that.</i>

10
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:14,233
<i>Just like what happened
in my car,</i>

11
00:00:14,367 --> 00:00:15,233
<i> where they found a gun.</i>

12
00:00:15,367 --> 00:00:16,700
<i> Only you can do that.</i>

13
00:00:16,833 --> 00:00:18,033
<i> Just remember, I warned you.</i>

14
00:00:18,167 --> 00:00:19,667
<i> Who's paying you now?</i>

15
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,600
<i>Are you a puppet
of the syndicates too?</i>

16
00:00:21,733 --> 00:00:24,100
<i>Thanks for what you did earlier.</i>

17
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:25,533
<i> Clarissa.</i>

18
00:00:25,667 --> 00:00:26,800
<i> I'm Yvette.</i>

19
00:00:26,933 --> 00:00:30,533
<i>We have upcoming medical
missions at our foundation.</i>

20
00:00:30,667 --> 00:00:32,300
<i> We need more volunteers.</i>

21
00:00:32,433 --> 00:00:33,500
<i> I've retrieved it.</i>

22
00:00:33,633 --> 00:00:35,700
<i> I've approached three experts.</i>

23
00:00:35,867 --> 00:00:38,533
<i>The flash drive
can't really be restored.</i>

24
00:00:38,667 --> 00:00:41,200
<i>What now? How are we going
to help father now?</i>

25
00:00:41,333 --> 00:00:43,133
<i>I just want to solve
our problems</i>

26
00:00:43,267 --> 00:00:44,900
<i> so we can be complete again.</i>

27
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:46,600
<i> But what are we going to do?</i>

28
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:49,600
<i>How can you earn
someone's trust?</i>

29
00:00:49,733 --> 00:00:50,933
<i> It's Golda.</i>

30
00:00:51,067 --> 00:00:56,733
<i>You have to earn someone's heart
first so they can trust you.</i>

31
00:00:56,867 --> 00:00:57,700
<i> I'll go outside.</i>

32
00:00:57,833 --> 00:00:58,367
<i> I'll come with you.</i>

33
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,100
<i> Me too!</i>

34
00:00:59,233 --> 00:01:00,167
<i> Get your keys.</i>

35
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,733
<i> Hurry up!</i>

36
00:01:01,867 --> 00:01:02,533
<i> Andrew!</i>

37
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:03,967
<i> JoeyOnDuty?</i>

38
00:01:04,100 --> 00:01:04,933
<i> What are you doing here?</i>

39
00:01:05,067 --> 00:01:06,733
<i> I need your help.</i>

40
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:07,600
<i> Help for what?</i>

41
00:01:07,733 --> 00:01:09,833
<i> I need to find Golda.</i>

42
00:01:30,700 --> 00:01:31,700
Joey!

43
00:01:31,833 --> 00:01:33,733
The car is ready.

44
00:01:33,867 --> 00:01:34,733
Let's go!

45
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:36,933
You know...

46
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:38,333
You know how girls are.

47
00:01:38,467 --> 00:01:40,100
You know, they take their time.

48
00:01:40,233 --> 00:01:41,933
Sometimes they want
to smell good, look good.

49
00:01:42,100 --> 00:01:44,167
- Maybe she's taking her time.
- It's already night.

50
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:45,333
It's late.

51
00:01:45,467 --> 00:01:46,633
Where's Joey?

52
00:01:48,033 --> 00:01:48,967
Hey, Joey!

53
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,067
Are you there?

54
00:01:51,433 --> 00:01:55,567
Oh my, I told you before,
didn't I?

55
00:01:55,700 --> 00:01:57,300
Don't look for someone
who's not here.

56
00:01:57,433 --> 00:02:00,467
Don't look for Joey
when I'm here.

57
00:02:01,767 --> 00:02:03,000
Lola, please.

58
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:04,367
That's enough.
Stop flirting around.

59
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,667
We're looking for Joey.
So noisy.

60
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:07,667
What's with you?

61
00:02:07,800 --> 00:02:10,000
She's gone!
She left a while ago.

62
00:02:11,333 --> 00:02:12,733
Do you know where she went?

63
00:02:14,667 --> 00:02:16,100
Where?

64
00:02:16,233 --> 00:02:20,200
Maybe she just wants
to leave alone.

65
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:25,267
Where did Joey go?

66
00:02:25,400 --> 00:02:26,933
What happened?

67
00:02:27,067 --> 00:02:29,467
Why do you suddenly need
my help?

68
00:02:30,767 --> 00:02:33,233
The flash drive
hasn't been restored...

69
00:02:34,933 --> 00:02:36,933
so the video is gone.

70
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,500
I need to talk to Golda.

71
00:02:43,667 --> 00:02:47,167
<i> Trust is based on feelings.</i>

72
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:54,333
<i>You need to win someone's heart
first so they can trust you.</i>

73
00:02:56,267 --> 00:02:59,533
Well, that's because
your flash drive

74
00:02:59,667 --> 00:03:01,900
looks like it can never be
repaired.

75
00:03:05,233 --> 00:03:07,233
Anyway...

76
00:03:07,367 --> 00:03:10,300
what do you need from Golda?

77
00:03:13,933 --> 00:03:15,867
I want to talk to her

78
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,133
so I can get her to admit

79
00:03:17,267 --> 00:03:20,000
that what happened between her
and father isn't true.

80
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:22,900
And so she can tell me
who really ordered her

81
00:03:23,067 --> 00:03:24,933
to discredit father like that.

82
00:03:26,233 --> 00:03:29,200
That would help father,
wouldn't it?

83
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:30,200
Please, Andrew.

84
00:03:30,333 --> 00:03:34,067
If I have to kneel
in front of you, I will.

85
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:36,100
Please, I'll do anything.

86
00:03:39,400 --> 00:03:40,500
Hey, Joey.

87
00:03:42,667 --> 00:03:45,367
You don't need to do that, okay?

88
00:03:47,433 --> 00:03:49,600
I know where Golda lives.

89
00:04:07,867 --> 00:04:09,333
Clarissa...

90
00:04:09,467 --> 00:04:10,100
Clarissa...

91
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:11,200
Diego.

92
00:04:16,267 --> 00:04:17,633
Diego, look at this.

93
00:04:17,767 --> 00:04:19,533
I'm being offered a job,

94
00:04:19,667 --> 00:04:22,400
and I'm thinking
about taking it. Look.

95
00:04:22,533 --> 00:04:23,367
Clarissa.

96
00:04:25,833 --> 00:04:30,733
Clarissa, there's something
I need to tell you.

97
00:04:30,900 --> 00:04:32,767
What is it?

98
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:34,400
Did something happen?

99
00:05:03,333 --> 00:05:05,233
<i> What are you going to say?</i>

100
00:05:05,367 --> 00:05:07,067
I'll be gone for a long time.

101
00:05:07,200 --> 00:05:09,500
I'll be assigned to Cebu.

102
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:13,467
Is that all?

103
00:05:14,767 --> 00:05:19,000
Yes, that's why I'm asking
for your forgiveness

104
00:05:19,133 --> 00:05:20,367
as early as now.

105
00:05:20,500 --> 00:05:25,033
Sorry if I'll be gone during
the time my friend needs me,

106
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:27,100
if I can't help with his case.

107
00:05:37,567 --> 00:05:38,767
This is for you.

108
00:05:40,467 --> 00:05:41,400
For me?

109
00:05:47,533 --> 00:05:49,400
Hey, Diego,
this is a huge amount.

110
00:05:49,533 --> 00:05:51,367
- I can't take this.
- No, no!

111
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:54,067
- No, no!
- Take it. Hide it. Use it.

112
00:05:54,200 --> 00:05:55,833
Use it, Clarissa.

113
00:05:55,967 --> 00:05:58,433
You need this
while Miguel is in jail.

114
00:06:01,200 --> 00:06:05,167
This is my payment for the sins
I committed against you.

115
00:06:05,300 --> 00:06:06,967
What are you saying?

116
00:06:33,133 --> 00:06:36,100
Clarissa, I haven't been honest
with your family.

117
00:06:38,267 --> 00:06:39,800
There are also...

118
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:43,167
There are also many things
I want to tell you face-to-face,

119
00:06:43,333 --> 00:06:45,333
but I can't.

120
00:06:45,467 --> 00:06:46,867
Maybe...

121
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:50,000
Maybe I'm afraid
of what you might say to me.

122
00:06:51,867 --> 00:06:52,967
But...

123
00:06:54,833 --> 00:06:56,600
Clarissa, believe me.

124
00:06:58,633 --> 00:07:00,733
I just want to let you know
that I did everything

125
00:07:00,867 --> 00:07:03,433
to protect your husband,

126
00:07:03,567 --> 00:07:05,567
even my godchild, Joey...

127
00:07:07,067 --> 00:07:08,867
because you are all important
to me.

128
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:10,367
You are all so important...

129
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:14,900
especially you.

130
00:07:15,067 --> 00:07:16,467
Matias, what's the news?

131
00:07:16,600 --> 00:07:19,600
Boss, I don't know if Parak
is being lazy.

132
00:07:21,033 --> 00:07:23,033
He's here at Delgado's house...

133
00:07:24,633 --> 00:07:26,700
but his target is not here.

134
00:07:26,833 --> 00:07:28,500
<i> Parak has his own strategy.</i>

135
00:07:28,633 --> 00:07:30,267
He doesn't need
to be guarded anymore.

136
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:33,767
What if he doesn't want to do
what you're asking him to do?

137
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:36,933
Maybe later he's crossing
two rivers.

138
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:41,133
Parak can't fight the group,
especially me.

139
00:07:41,267 --> 00:07:43,800
He knows better than
to double-cross us.

140
00:07:43,933 --> 00:07:47,000
So don't waste your time on him.

141
00:07:47,133 --> 00:07:48,700
Is that clear?

142
00:07:48,867 --> 00:07:49,800
Yes, Boss.

143
00:07:50,833 --> 00:07:51,800
Go ahead.

144
00:08:07,967 --> 00:08:09,800
<i> Diego,</i>

145
00:08:09,933 --> 00:08:12,000
you're important.

146
00:08:12,133 --> 00:08:13,967
You're important to us.

147
00:08:15,700 --> 00:08:18,800
You know, even if you're
my husband's best friend...

148
00:08:20,067 --> 00:08:22,567
I consider you as a true friend.

149
00:08:27,100 --> 00:08:31,633
So if you have a problem,
I'm right here.

150
00:08:31,767 --> 00:08:34,533
Maybe I can help you.

151
00:08:34,667 --> 00:08:36,100
No, I can do this.

152
00:08:38,300 --> 00:08:43,433
Just promise me that
you'll be careful, okay?

153
00:08:43,567 --> 00:08:46,167
And Joey too, take care of her.

154
00:08:48,067 --> 00:08:49,267
And what I want, Clarissa,

155
00:08:49,400 --> 00:08:51,467
is for you and my best friend
to be happy.

156
00:08:51,600 --> 00:08:54,367
Be a happy family when
he's released from jail, okay?

157
00:08:56,233 --> 00:08:57,500
Is that possible?

158
00:09:26,900 --> 00:09:28,100
Golda's not here.

159
00:09:28,267 --> 00:09:31,733
Joey, let's just go back
when she's back.

160
00:09:33,267 --> 00:09:35,233
Why does it seem like
she's not coming back?

161
00:09:40,833 --> 00:09:41,967
It seems like...

162
00:09:43,233 --> 00:09:44,633
she left in a hurry.

163
00:09:45,667 --> 00:09:47,733
The question is,
where is she going?

164
00:10:27,567 --> 00:10:28,833
<i>I'm just here to ask you
something.</i>

165
00:10:28,967 --> 00:10:32,100
<i>What's your relationship
with Major Miguel Delgado?</i>

166
00:10:55,433 --> 00:10:57,633
This isn't Golda's.

167
00:10:57,767 --> 00:10:59,200
I wonder who owns this.

168
00:11:05,433 --> 00:11:06,967
It seems like there's still
no one here.

169
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:11,333
It's better if we just
come back tomorrow.

170
00:11:11,467 --> 00:11:13,467
We've been here every night.

171
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:15,100
Don't complain anymore.

172
00:11:15,233 --> 00:11:18,400
Let's just follow
Parak's orders.

173
00:11:18,533 --> 00:11:19,500
Let's go.

174
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:22,800
What's that?

175
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:29,333
It seems like someone
is already there.

176
00:11:29,467 --> 00:11:30,867
I think Golda is there!

177
00:11:36,733 --> 00:11:40,267
Parak is the topnotcher
in his batch.

178
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:43,233
That's why Delgado
is so impressed with him.

179
00:11:50,567 --> 00:11:55,533
I now know why Parak can't seem
to eliminate Delgado.

180
00:11:57,333 --> 00:11:59,900
Matias, look at this.

181
00:12:04,433 --> 00:12:06,067
They're batchmates.

182
00:12:06,200 --> 00:12:09,133
Hence, they're friends.

183
00:12:09,267 --> 00:12:13,733
That's why even Delgado's
wife knows Parak.

184
00:12:13,867 --> 00:12:16,133
You know, Lisa,
I'm also impressed by Parak.

185
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,933
He's been keeping this secret
from us for so long.

186
00:12:21,267 --> 00:12:22,667
So what?

187
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,967
Are you going to report this
to Berdugo?

188
00:12:29,867 --> 00:12:32,133
Parak's happy days are over.

189
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:13,867
Have you heard anything?

190
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,100
Nothing.

191
00:13:26,500 --> 00:13:27,833
Hello, Parak?

192
00:13:27,967 --> 00:13:30,100
I just wanted to give you all
a heads-up.

193
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:32,267
<i> We're aborting our operations.</i>

194
00:13:33,633 --> 00:13:34,967
Do you copy?

195
00:13:35,100 --> 00:13:36,000
Abort.

196
00:13:36,133 --> 00:13:36,867
<i> Copy, Parak.</i>

197
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:37,967
But why?

198
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:40,833
Well, our service to Berdugo
is negative.

199
00:13:40,967 --> 00:13:42,400
We'll stop now.

200
00:13:42,533 --> 00:13:44,067
<i> But don't worry,</i>

201
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:47,467
you'll still receive
your final payment.

202
00:13:47,600 --> 00:13:48,233
Let's go.

203
00:13:48,367 --> 00:13:50,167
Parak said abort the operation.

204
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:06,800
Are they gone?

205
00:14:10,967 --> 00:14:11,900
They're gone.

206
00:14:13,867 --> 00:14:17,300
Joey, even though we don't have
a clue where Golda went...

207
00:14:23,133 --> 00:14:24,867
well, we do have this.

208
00:14:27,967 --> 00:14:30,200
I think we can still get
some information,

209
00:14:30,333 --> 00:14:33,900
just to find out
who it is from.

210
00:14:34,033 --> 00:14:37,533
Did you hear the name mentioned
earlier?

211
00:14:37,667 --> 00:14:38,800
Parak.

212
00:14:38,933 --> 00:14:41,767
I heard that, too,
when Ramon Orbos died.

213
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:43,433
I heard that there.

214
00:14:43,567 --> 00:14:45,833
<i>And you really planned
to hide from us?</i>

215
00:14:45,967 --> 00:14:51,000
<i>No, Madam, no!
I really came here to see Parak.</i>

216
00:14:51,133 --> 00:14:52,633
Do you know anything about that?

217
00:14:52,767 --> 00:14:54,833
Do you really want
to know the truth?

218
00:14:56,633 --> 00:14:58,300
Come with me.

219
00:14:58,433 --> 00:15:00,133
Let's go see your father.

220
00:15:20,433 --> 00:15:21,467
Can you still do it?

221
00:15:22,800 --> 00:15:27,300
I told you to rest here
in the car.

222
00:15:27,433 --> 00:15:28,900
No, I can do it.

223
00:15:31,667 --> 00:15:32,633
Coffee.

224
00:15:36,567 --> 00:15:37,667
Thank you.

225
00:15:42,033 --> 00:15:43,267
Sandwich too.

226
00:15:50,367 --> 00:15:51,400
Don't worry.

227
00:15:53,767 --> 00:15:55,700
Visiting hours
are about to start.

228
00:15:55,833 --> 00:15:58,167
It means, we can go in.

229
00:16:00,200 --> 00:16:01,300
Thank you.

230
00:16:04,000 --> 00:16:05,167
For what?

231
00:16:08,100 --> 00:16:11,567
For helping me find Golda.

232
00:16:11,733 --> 00:16:14,633
I really expected
that you'd ignore me.

233
00:16:14,767 --> 00:16:17,400
That's why I was so ready
to kneel in front of you

234
00:16:17,533 --> 00:16:18,867
so you'd agree.

235
00:16:20,333 --> 00:16:21,433
That's nothing.

236
00:16:21,567 --> 00:16:23,200
I wanted to help.

237
00:16:25,833 --> 00:16:28,200
You're really kind, too.

238
00:16:30,267 --> 00:16:32,100
But don't get used to it

239
00:16:32,233 --> 00:16:35,967
because the next time I give you
a sandwich and a coffee,

240
00:16:36,100 --> 00:16:37,733
I might charge you.

241
00:16:39,267 --> 00:16:40,267
Okay.

242
00:16:52,767 --> 00:16:53,933
Peter.

243
00:16:54,067 --> 00:16:55,300
<i> Joey!</i>

244
00:16:55,433 --> 00:16:57,067
<i>Joey, you're really
something else!</i>

245
00:16:57,200 --> 00:17:00,033
You left us so suddenly,
and you're not home yet.

246
00:17:00,167 --> 00:17:01,233
Where are you?

247
00:17:04,400 --> 00:17:05,233
Hey!

248
00:17:05,367 --> 00:17:07,100
Why did you leave without us?

249
00:17:07,233 --> 00:17:09,067
<i>- You know it's dangerous!
- That's right!</i>

250
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:12,233
You even tricked us
so we can't be with you, right?

251
00:17:12,367 --> 00:17:13,500
<i> You're too much.</i>

252
00:17:13,633 --> 00:17:16,500
Sorry, I have something
to do alone.

253
00:17:17,733 --> 00:17:19,233
You should've brought me
with you.

254
00:17:19,367 --> 00:17:20,967
<i> Well...</i>

255
00:17:21,100 --> 00:17:24,867
Don't worry about her because
as long as she's with me,

256
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:29,233
she's safe even without you,
guys.

257
00:17:30,067 --> 00:17:32,900
Oh my, you didn't bring us,
but Boss Budol is there?

258
00:17:33,033 --> 00:17:35,033
He's the one who can help me!

259
00:17:35,167 --> 00:17:37,467
And tell Jin Ho,

260
00:17:37,600 --> 00:17:39,667
<i>I didn't bring you because you
were making a lot of noise!</i>

261
00:17:39,800 --> 00:17:41,133
You're both noisy!

262
00:17:41,267 --> 00:17:43,900
Just because of that,
you left us?

263
00:17:44,033 --> 00:17:45,333
You know, I explained it
already.

264
00:17:45,467 --> 00:17:48,300
That's okay. Stop it.
I'm sleepy.

265
00:17:53,867 --> 00:17:55,500
Thank you for coming.

266
00:17:57,300 --> 00:18:00,700
I know you're going through
something.

267
00:18:00,833 --> 00:18:02,433
Andrew told me.

268
00:18:04,967 --> 00:18:07,600
Father, I'm sorry if I'm being
stubborn right now.

269
00:18:09,033 --> 00:18:13,533
I was just looking for a way
for you to be released.

270
00:18:13,667 --> 00:18:18,833
That's why I asked Andrew
to help me find Golda.

271
00:18:18,967 --> 00:18:21,367
Did you talk to her?

272
00:18:21,500 --> 00:18:23,100
Unfortunately, no.

273
00:18:24,533 --> 00:18:27,400
She wasn't at her house
when we went.

274
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,533
But we found this.

275
00:18:39,633 --> 00:18:41,100
I know this.

276
00:18:41,233 --> 00:18:43,700
This is exactly what
that person is using.

277
00:18:43,833 --> 00:18:45,400
Do you know him, Father?

278
00:18:46,567 --> 00:18:47,567
Who is it?

279
00:18:47,700 --> 00:18:49,833
This is the reason why
I wanted you to come here.

280
00:18:49,967 --> 00:18:51,300
Talk to your father,

281
00:18:51,433 --> 00:18:54,733
so he can explain the truth
to you.

282
00:18:54,900 --> 00:18:56,033
Because if it were me,

283
00:18:56,167 --> 00:18:58,933
you definitely
wouldn't believe it.

284
00:19:01,700 --> 00:19:05,067
What's the truth? I'm confused.

285
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,900
Joey...

286
00:19:07,033 --> 00:19:09,200
your Godfather Diego
betrayed us.

287
00:19:10,700 --> 00:19:12,733
He's the protector
of the syndicates...

288
00:19:14,300 --> 00:19:16,600
and he's the one they call
"Parak."

289
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:25,600
I'm so glad you came.
Have a seat.

290
00:19:26,100 --> 00:19:27,400
Thank you.

291
00:19:31,400 --> 00:19:35,033
Your organization is impressive.

292
00:19:35,167 --> 00:19:37,333
I'm sure you've helped a lot.

293
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:39,733
We try as much as we can.

294
00:19:39,867 --> 00:19:42,833
Thank you for accepting the job.

295
00:19:42,967 --> 00:19:45,900
Ma'am, I should be the one
who should thank you.

296
00:19:46,033 --> 00:19:49,467
Apart from the fact
that I'll be busy,

297
00:19:49,600 --> 00:19:52,067
I have the opportunity
to help others.

298
00:19:52,200 --> 00:19:58,000
Ma'am, is it hard to run
such a big organization?

299
00:19:58,133 --> 00:20:00,300
A bit, but you know,

300
00:20:00,433 --> 00:20:03,667
it's fulfilling and also
I'm not alone,

301
00:20:03,833 --> 00:20:08,700
thanks to my sponsors
and to my family.

302
00:20:14,400 --> 00:20:15,567
That's my husband.

303
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:22,033
Do you know Boss Budol?

304
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:26,700
I mean, Boss Idol.

305
00:20:26,833 --> 00:20:28,433
Are you close?

306
00:20:28,567 --> 00:20:30,067
You can say that.

307
00:20:30,200 --> 00:20:31,900
He's my brother.

308
00:20:33,933 --> 00:20:36,433
Your Godfather Diego
betrayed us.

309
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:38,667
He is the one they call "Parak."

310
00:20:39,967 --> 00:20:40,800
What?

311
00:20:43,600 --> 00:20:45,733
That is impossible. Godfather?

312
00:20:45,867 --> 00:20:47,133
I'm sure.

313
00:20:48,733 --> 00:20:50,900
We were face-to-face.

314
00:20:51,033 --> 00:20:53,400
It came straight from his mouth.

315
00:20:53,533 --> 00:20:57,767
He didn't admit it,
but he couldn't deny the truth.

316
00:20:57,900 --> 00:20:59,267
How could that happen?

317
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,567
Do you know,

318
00:21:00,700 --> 00:21:03,667
he even helped me fix my flash
drive so I could get the video?

319
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:07,633
Video that wasn't recovered...

320
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:08,533
right?

321
00:21:09,667 --> 00:21:11,367
So are you saying it's not true

322
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:13,400
that my flash drive
wasn't fixed?

323
00:21:14,433 --> 00:21:15,567
What I'm saying is,

324
00:21:15,700 --> 00:21:18,067
if he were a part
of the syndicate,

325
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:22,000
I'm sure he wouldn't want
the video to be released

326
00:21:22,133 --> 00:21:24,967
because that can be taken
against them.

327
00:21:26,367 --> 00:21:27,533
Father,

328
00:21:27,667 --> 00:21:29,067
you know that godfather is like
a second father to me, right?

329
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:31,033
He can't do that to us.

330
00:21:31,167 --> 00:21:33,700
Godfather can't do that.

331
00:21:33,833 --> 00:21:35,333
What you're saying
is impossible.

332
00:21:35,467 --> 00:21:36,600
That's not true.

333
00:21:39,633 --> 00:21:40,533
Father?

334
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:09,733
How do you plead?

335
00:22:09,867 --> 00:22:11,033
Not guilty, Your Honor.

336
00:22:11,167 --> 00:22:12,833
We move for the grant of bail.

337
00:22:12,967 --> 00:22:13,733
Are you giving up?

338
00:22:13,867 --> 00:22:14,500
Not now.

339
00:22:14,633 --> 00:22:16,233
I know someone who can help us.

340
00:22:16,400 --> 00:22:19,567
If you have tracked me down,
probably, so have they!

341
00:22:19,700 --> 00:22:21,233
I just want father to be freed.

342
00:22:21,367 --> 00:22:22,933
We know everything,
so just admit it.

343
00:22:23,067 --> 00:22:23,833
Remember the order.

344
00:22:23,967 --> 00:22:26,000
Kill Diego, so surround
the house.

345
00:22:26,133 --> 00:22:27,133
Are you done with Parak?

346
00:22:27,267 --> 00:22:28,000
Looks like he's with someone,
Boss.

347
00:22:28,133 --> 00:22:29,533
Damn it!

348
00:22:29,667 --> 00:22:30,800
Go ahead, I'll take care of it!

349
00:22:30,933 --> 00:22:31,900
It's a great story.

350
00:22:32,033 --> 00:22:34,867
Romance-turned-crime duo.

351
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:36,233
It's like a drama series.

352
00:22:36,367 --> 00:22:38,100
They make people disappear.

353
00:22:38,233 --> 00:22:40,533
So you're saying
he's really gone?
